<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gdańsk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gdańsk (Danzig) is a port on the Baltic coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. It was the main outlet for the grain exports of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>, shipping <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rye">rye</a>, wheat and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a> to western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, and its trade enriched the Polish nobility.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gdansk.jpg" alt="Gdańsk" width="320" height="174" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Delso · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Calle_Dlugie_Pobrzeze,_Gdansk,_Polonia,_2013-05-20,_DD_06.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
